<title>BELGIUM: EU ministers agree excessive deficit reports.</title>
<headline>EU ministers agree excessive deficit reports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union finance ministers on Monday agreed a series of official reports for nine countries that found them running budget deficits in excess of those required by the Maastrict treaty, minister said.</p>
<p>Finland and the Netherlands were dropped off the so-called excessive deficit list, joining Denmark, Luxembourg and Ireland. No report was issued for Britain in order to allow the new government to issue a budget first.</p>
</text>
